  "review": {
    "status": "revise",
    "summary": "The recovery_exit leaf has an incorrect recovery predicate. The active recovery is caused by damage and low health (health 5.0), not low supplies. The criteria require food >= 7, but the body already has food 18, and the hazard is health, not starvation. The recovery criteria should require health above a safe threshold (e.g., >10) and alive, but should not impose a food minimum that is not part of the active hazard. Additionally, the recovery leaf's position criteria (floor at y=30, air at y=32/33) are consistent with the current body cells, but the food criterion is an incorrect predicate for this recovery type. Revise the recovery_exit criteria to remove the food minimum and focus on health and safe landing.",
    "target_id": "recovery_exit"
  },
